homelab-mail-proxy (0.1.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Ship backup-paths.txt (this package's own conf.d file + systemd
    drop-in only, never the rest of a shared proxy host's /etc/haproxy)
    for homelab-borg-service-backup-client's homelab_only auto-discovery.

 -- Gardner <gardner@homelab>  Sun, 23 Aug 2026 18:00:00 -0500

homelab-mail-proxy (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release. HAProxy TCP passthrough for the 6 mail-related
    ports (SMTP/SMTPS/Submission/Roundcube-SMTPS-optional/IMAP/IMAPS),
    templated backend hosts (may run on a different server than the
    services it fronts). Config lives entirely in its own conf.d drop-in
    plus a systemd EXTRAOPTS override -- never edits haproxy.cfg or
    /etc/default/haproxy, verified empirically not to work reliably on a
    real HAProxy 3.2.9 install.

 -- Gardner <gardner@homelab>  Sun, 23 Aug 2026 05:00:00 -0500
